# =============================================================================
# .trivyignore
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trivy exceptions, read by:
#   - the "Trivy image scan" step in .github/workflows/docker.yml (vulnerabilities, ids like CVE-2026-1234)
#   - the "trivy config" step in .github/workflows/terraform-pr.yml (misconfigurations, ids like AVD-AZU-0012)
# Both scans fail on HIGH and CRITICAL findings (the image scan only on findings that have a fix).
#
# Add a line only when a finding is truly not actionable, and every line needs (1) a comment above it
# saying why, and (2) an expiry so it cannot be forgotten:
#
#   # openssl CVE affects only the DTLS path, which this app does not use. Revisit when the
#   # base image updates.
#   CVE-2026-1234 exp:2026-12-31
#
# Prefer fixing the cause: rebuild to pick up a newer base image, bump the dependency, or change the
# Terraform. Never lower the scan severity to make a finding go away.
# =============================================================================

# --- Litestream 0.5.17 (usr/local/bin/litestream) -------------------------------------------------
# Found by the first image scan. These are Go libraries compiled into the official Litestream binary,
# which is pinned by checksum in the Dockerfile. 0.5.17 is the latest release (checked 2026-09-21), so
# there is no fixed binary to move to. This deployment uses only Litestream's Azure Blob replica: it
# never uses the SFTP replica (golang.org/x/crypto/ssh) and never runs or connects to a gRPC service
# (google.golang.org/grpc), so those code paths are not used here. Reachability of the golang.org/x/net
# finding was NOT analysed; it is waived on the same basis (no fixed binary exists) and is the first
# one to check. Revisit at the expiry, or as soon as Litestream publishes a release with updated modules
# (then bump LITESTREAM_VERSION and both checksums in the Dockerfile and litestream-integration.yml).
CVE-2026-56854 exp:2026-10-31
CVE-2026-46600 exp:2026-10-31
CVE-2026-84304 exp:2026-10-31
CVE-2026-84445 exp:2026-10-31
